    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Inaugural Plight\nIberia\nAIR LINES OF SPAIN\nAUGUST, 1954\nMADRID • NEW YORK • MADRID\n462nd Anniversary of start of Columbus'\nVoyage of Discovery of America\nES\n-2AG0\nLESTANA\nPERREOS\nMADRIE\nIBERIA Air Lines\n339 Madison Aven\nNew York 17, N.\n20\nI CTS.\nMATE\nCANA\nICO DIE\nVI\n-2AG054\noys.\nCORREQ AEREO\nPRIMER\nVUELO DIRECTO\nberin\nAGOSTO\n•S.A.\n1954\nMADRE\nA NUEVA YORE\nPRINTED IN U.S. A.",
      "AIR\nMain Office:\nPlaza de Canovas 4\nMadrid, Spain\nberia\nE\nS\nF\nMember, Internafional Air Transport Association (I.A.T.A.)\n339 MADISON AVENUE • NEW YORK CITY 17\nMUrray Hill 9-7390\nSPAIN\nCable address:\nIBERIAVION\nIn reply, refer to\nI BERIA LINEAS AEREAS ESPANOLAS\nMadrid, Spain\nAugust 3, 1954\nThis cover is being\nsent you on IBERIA'S Inaugural Flight of\nits direct service between Madrid and New York.\nWe sincerely\nhope you will find it an interesting memento of our initial\nflight on the 462nd Anniversary of the start of Columbus!\nVoyage of Discovery of America.\nThe airplane bringing you the memento is one of a fleet of 3\nLockheed Super E Constellations -- named the Nina, the\nand the Santa Maria, in memory of Christopher Columbus! own\nships. For that reason, IBERIA'S New York -- Madrid service\nis known as \"The Route of the Sky Caravels.\"\nThe Lockheed aircraft is the newest type of Super Constellation.\nThe faster turbo-compound engines, more spacious cabins and a\nrevolutionary luxury interior give these latest Constellations\nunequalled passenger appeal and operating efficiency. IBERIA'S\nfleet provides a blend of speed, luxury and comfort which con-\nstitutes a new concept of air travel.\nOur thanks for your interest in IBERIA, and our sincere hope\nthat this philatelic memento will please you.\nIBERIA\nAir Lines of Spain\nLITHO IN U.S.A.\nHEROUTEOFTHE SKY\nCARAVE"
    ],
